<section class="formula" aria-label="Exercise plus Evidence equals Clearer Decision"><div class="wrap"><div class="f-item"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-puzzle"/></svg><span>Exercise</span></div><span class="f-sign" aria-hidden="true">+</span><div class="f-item"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-list"/></svg><span>Evidence</span></div><span class="f-sign" aria-hidden="true">=</span><div class="f-item"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" style="overflow:hidden"><g class="mini-ship"><use href="#i-rocket"/></g><path d="M4 22.5c1-1.800 2.600-2 4-1.200 1-1.600 2.800-1.600 4 0 1.200-1.600 3-1.600 4 0 1.400-.8 3-.6 4 1.200" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.45" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Clearer Decision</span></div></div><p class="take">When people are in the right role, their career can take off.</p></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Same method, two purposes</div><h2>What is the centre for?</h2><p class="intro">Both use realistic exercises and trained observers. What changes is the question you are answering and what people receive afterwards.</p>
<div class="purpose-grid">
<article class="purpose"><svg class="p-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-profile"/></svg><span class="q">Who should we hire?</span><h3>Assessment Centre</h3><p>See how people think, communicate and respond in situations like the real job, then compare the evidence against what the role needs.</p><p class="out"><strong>You receive:</strong> a clear recommendation, the evidence behind it, any gaps and onboarding priorities.</p></article>
<article class="purpose dev"><svg class="p-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-stairs"/></svg><span class="q">How do we grow our people?</span><h3>Development Centre</h3><p>Give your people a chance to practise, get useful feedback and understand what to build next. There is no pass or fail.</p><p class="out"><strong>You receive:</strong> strengths, development priorities and the support that will help.</p></article>
</div><p class="note">We agree the purpose and who sees the findings before the centre begins, so people know what they are taking part in and findings are not later used for something else.</p></div></section>
<section class="section roles"><div class="wrap"><svg class="sec-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-target"/></svg><div class="eyebrow">Built around the role</div><h2>One approach, shaped for your people.</h2><p class="intro">Every centre starts with what the role needs. Choose a group to see how the exercises could change.</p>
<div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Choose a group of roles">
<button class="tab" role="tab" id="t-sales" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="p-sales">Sales</button>
<button class="tab" role="tab" id="t-eng" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="p-eng" tabindex="-1">Engineers</button>
<button class="tab" role="tab" id="t-cs" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="p-cs" tabindex="-1">Customer service</button>
<button class="tab" role="tab" id="t-tal" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="p-tal" tabindex="-1">Emerging talent</button>
</div>
<div class="role-panel" role="tabpanel" id="p-sales" aria-labelledby="t-sales"><div><span class="mini">Group business case</span><p>Prioritise customer opportunities and propose a 30-day territory plan.</p></div><div><span class="mini">One-to-one role play</span><p>Meet a customer, explore what they need and respond to their objections.</p></div><div><span class="mini">What we might look for</span><ul><li>Understanding needs</li><li>Commercial reasoning</li><li>Clear communication</li><li>Resilience</li></ul></div></div>
<div class="role-panel" role="tabpanel" id="p-eng" aria-labelledby="t-eng" hidden><div><span class="mini">Group business case</span><p>Investigate a recurring fault and recommend a fix within a limited budget.</p></div><div><span class="mini">One-to-one role play</span><p>Explain a technical risk to a manager without a technical background.</p></div><div><span class="mini">What we might look for</span><ul><li>Structured problem solving</li><li>Safety and quality judgement</li><li>Clear explanation</li><li>Collaboration</li></ul></div></div>
<div class="role-panel" role="tabpanel" id="p-cs" aria-labelledby="t-cs" hidden><div><span class="mini">Group business case</span><p>Review a service process after complaints rise, and agree what to change first.</p></div><div><span class="mini">One-to-one role play</span><p>Help an unhappy customer while working within company policy.</p></div><div><span class="mini">What we might look for</span><ul><li>Empathy</li><li>Ownership</li><li>Problem solving</li><li>Composure</li></ul></div></div>
<div class="role-panel" role="tabpanel" id="p-tal" aria-labelledby="t-tal" hidden><div><span class="mini">Group business case</span><p>Work through a business challenge and present a recommendation to a panel.</p></div><div><span class="mini">One-to-one role play</span><p>Hold a difficult conversation with a team member.</p></div><div><span class="mini">What we might look for</span><ul><li>Reasoning and judgement</li><li>Influence</li><li>Developing others</li><li>Willingness to learn</li></ul></div></div>
<p class="small">These are examples only. Exercises and criteria are agreed with your team.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap"><svg class="sec-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-speech"/></svg><div class="eyebrow">How a day works</div><h2>Evidence from more than one moment.</h2><p class="intro">Seeing someone in different situations gives a fuller picture than one interview can. A typical day brings these moments together.</p>
<div class="day-grid">
<article class="day"><div class="day-img"><svg class="scene" viewBox="0 0 240 150" role="img" aria-label="Three people working together at a table"><g stroke="#2c2a26" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" fill="none"><circle cx="70" cy="53" r="9" fill="#fff"/><path d="M54 90v-8a16 16 0 0 1 32 0v8z" fill="#f3dfb0"/><circle cx="120" cy="53" r="9" fill="#fff"/><path d="M104 90v-8a16 16 0 0 1 32 0v8z" fill="#f8dc8c"/><circle cx="170" cy="53" r="9" fill="#fff"/><path d="M154 90v-8a16 16 0 0 1 32 0v8z" fill="#cfe0c9"/><path d="M32 92h176" stroke-width="5"/><path d="M52 92v44M188 92v44"/><path d="M154 3h54a8 8 0 0 1 8 8v10a8 8 0 0 1-8 8H172l-8 9v-9H154a8 8 0 0 1-8-8v-10a8 8 0 0 1 8-8z" fill="#fff"/><path d="M160 16h.01M180 16h.01M200 16h.01" stroke-width="4"/><path d="M10 138h220"/></g></svg></div><div class="day-txt"><h3>Think and work together</h3><p>People think on their own first, then work as a group on a shared business case.</p></div></article>
<article class="day"><div class="day-img"><svg class="scene" viewBox="0 0 240 150" role="img" aria-label="A person presenting a chart to two seated people"><g stroke="#2c2a26" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" fill="none"><rect x="16" y="16" width="104" height="72" rx="3" fill="#fff"/><path d="M34 70V54M54 70V42M74 70V34M94 70V48" stroke="#356767" stroke-width="7"/><path d="M68 88v48M44 136l24-20 24 20"/><circle cx="150" cy="31" r="9" fill="#fff"/><path d="M134 68v-8a16 16 0 0 1 32 0v8z" fill="#f8dc8c"/><path d="M134 56L112 46"/><circle cx="182" cy="91.2" r="7.2" fill="#fff"/><path d="M169.2 120.80000000000001v-6.4a12.8 12.8 0 0 1 25.6 0v6.4z" fill="#f3dfb0"/><circle cx="218" cy="91.2" r="7.2" fill="#fff"/><path d="M205.2 120.80000000000001v-6.4a12.8 12.8 0 0 1 25.6 0v6.4z" fill="#cfe0c9"/><path d="M10 138h220"/></g></svg></div><div class="day-txt"><h3>Present and explain</h3><p>Each group presents to assessors, then individuals answer questions on their own reasoning.</p></div></article>
<article class="day"><div class="day-img"><svg class="scene" viewBox="0 0 240 150" role="img" aria-label="Two people in a one-to-one conversation"><g stroke="#2c2a26" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" fill="none"><circle cx="68" cy="60.35" r="10.35" fill="#fff"/><path d="M49.6 102.89999999999999v-9.2a18.4 18.4 0 0 1 36.8 0v9.2z" fill="#f3dfb0"/><circle cx="172" cy="60.35" r="10.35" fill="#fff"/><path d="M153.6 102.89999999999999v-9.2a18.4 18.4 0 0 1 36.8 0v9.2z" fill="#f8dc8c"/><path d="M26 8h76a8 8 0 0 1 8 8v16a8 8 0 0 1-8 8H100l-8 9v-9H26a8 8 0 0 1-8-8v-16a8 8 0 0 1 8-8z" fill="#f6efdf"/><path d="M32 24h64"/><path d="M138 8h76a8 8 0 0 1 8 8v16a8 8 0 0 1-8 8H156l-8 9v-9H138a8 8 0 0 1-8-8v-16a8 8 0 0 1 8-8z" fill="#fbf2dc"/><path d="M146 24h60"/><path d="M10 138h220"/></g></svg></div><div class="day-txt"><h3>Handle a real conversation</h3><p>A one-to-one role play shows how each person responds in the moment, followed by a short debrief.</p></div></article>
<article class="day"><div class="day-img"><svg class="scene" viewBox="0 0 240 150" role="img" aria-label="Two assessors with a shared scoring sheet"><g stroke="#2c2a26" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" fill="none"><rect x="84" y="14" width="74" height="122" rx="5" fill="#fff"/><path d="M104 14v-5h34v5"/><g fill="#f0b429" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="102" cy="42" r="5"/><circle cx="118" cy="42" r="5"/><circle cx="134" cy="42" r="5"/><circle cx="102" cy="68" r="5"/><circle cx="118" cy="68" r="5"/><circle cx="102" cy="94" r="5"/><circle cx="118" cy="94" r="5"/><circle cx="134" cy="94" r="5"/></g><path d="M100 118h42"/><circle cx="42" cy="69.9" r="9.9" fill="#fff"/><path d="M24.4 110.60000000000001v-8.8a17.6 17.6 0 0 1 35.2 0v8.8z" fill="#f3dfb0"/><circle cx="200" cy="69.9" r="9.9" fill="#fff"/><path d="M182.4 110.60000000000001v-8.8a17.6 17.6 0 0 1 35.2 0v8.8z" fill="#cfe0c9"/><path d="M10 138h220"/></g></svg></div><div class="day-txt"><h3>Bring the evidence together</h3><p>Assessors rate independently first, then discuss the evidence and agree one view of each person.</p></div></article>
</div><p class="line-note">One format can take 12 participants through a day in three groups. Numbers, length and exercises depend on your roles and available assessors.</p></div></section>
<section class="section fair"><div class="wrap fair-grid"><div><svg class="sec-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-list"/></svg><div class="eyebrow">Fair by design</div><h2>The same chance for everyone.</h2><p class="intro">A centre is only useful if you can trust the evidence. These safeguards are built in from the start.</p></div>
<ul>
<li>Everyone receives the same brief, timing and scoring guide.</li>
<li>Assessors are trained in what to look for and how to record it.</li>
<li>Role-players follow agreed responses, so each person gets a fair test.</li>
<li>Ratings are recorded independently before the panel discusses them.</li>
<li>Each person is seen across several sources of evidence.</li>
<li>Your organisation always makes the final decision.</li>
</ul></div></section>
<section class="section" id="deliverables"><div class="wrap"><svg class="sec-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-board"/></svg><div class="eyebrow">What you receive</div><h2>Everything your team needs.</h2><p class="intro">These samples show the kinds of materials we create. All names, scores and content below are made up for illustration.</p>
<div class="show-grid">
<article class="item"><div class="sheet"><span class="stamp">Sample</span><div class="sh-t">Assessment Framework</div><div class="sh-s">Customer Advisor, entry level</div><table class="st"><tr><th>Competency</th><th>What we would see</th></tr><tr><td>Understanding needs</td><td>Asks open questions before suggesting a solution</td></tr><tr><td>Reasoning</td><td>Explains why, using the facts available</td></tr><tr><td>Communication</td><td>Adapts the message to the listener</td></tr><tr><td>Resilience</td><td>Stays constructive after a “no”</td></tr><tr><td>Teamwork</td><td>Builds on others’ ideas</td></tr></table></div><h3>Assessment framework</h3><p>Agreed competencies, observable behaviours and scoring benchmarks for your role.</p></article>
<article class="item"><div class="sheet"><span class="stamp">Sample</span><div class="sh-t">Participant Brief</div><div class="sh-s">Group business case · 75 minutes</div><div class="sh-l">Your situation</div><p style="font-size:11px;color:inherit;line-height:1.45">You have joined the team at Riverside Supplies. Three customers need attention, and there is only time for one this month.</p><div class="sh-l">Your task</div><p style="font-size:11px;color:inherit;line-height:1.45">Agree which customer comes first, then prepare a short plan to present.</p><div class="sh-box"><strong>Everyone presents.</strong> Be ready to explain your own thinking.</div></div><h3>Participant materials</h3><p>The business case, preparation instructions, group task and presentation requirements.</p></article>
<article class="item"><div class="sheet"><span class="stamp">Sample</span><div class="sh-t">Role-Play Pack</div><div class="sh-s">Role-player guide · 20 minutes</div><div class="bubble">“We’re happy with our current supplier.”</div><div class="bubble r"><strong>If asked why:</strong> share the late-delivery concern.</div><div class="bubble">“Your price looks higher.”</div><div class="bubble r"><strong>Only if they ask about value:</strong> mention service hours.</div><div class="sh-l">Debrief prompt</div><p style="font-size:11px;color:inherit">What would you do differently?</p></div><h3>Role-play pack</h3><p>The briefing, customer script, rules for sharing information, agreed objections and debrief prompts.</p></article>
<article class="item"><div class="sheet"><span class="stamp">Sample</span><div class="sh-t">Assessor Scoring Sheet</div><div class="sh-s">Participant 04 · Role play</div><table class="st"><tr><th>Behaviour</th><th>Rating</th></tr><tr><td>Explores needs before offering</td><td class="dots">●●●○</td></tr><tr><td>Responds to objections calmly</td><td class="dots">●●●●</td></tr><tr><td>Links product to customer value</td><td class="dots">●●○○</td></tr></table><div class="sh-l">Evidence, in their words and actions</div><div class="sh-box">Asked “What matters most to you?” before discussing price.</div></div><h3>Assessor toolkit</h3><p>Observation forms, scoring sheets, behavioural anchors, probing guidance and a calibration template.</p></article>
<article class="item"><div class="sheet"><span class="stamp">Sample</span><div class="sh-t">Delivery Guide</div><div class="sh-s">Room plan · 12 participants</div><table class="st"><tr><th>Room</th><th>09:00</th><th>10:30</th><th>13:00</th><th>14:00</th></tr><tr><td>Briefing</td><td class="slot a">All</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Room A</td><td class="slot b">Group 1</td><td class="slot b">Present</td><td class="slot d">Role play</td><td class="slot d">Role play</td></tr><tr><td>Room B</td><td class="slot c">Group 2</td><td class="slot c">Present</td><td class="slot d">Role play</td><td class="slot d">Role play</td></tr><tr><td>Room C</td><td class="slot a">Group 3</td><td class="slot a">Present</td><td class="slot d">Role play</td><td class="slot d">Role play</td></tr></table><div class="sh-l">Before the day</div><div class="sh-box">☑ Rooms booked &nbsp; ☑ Assessors paired &nbsp; ☐ Packs printed</div></div><h3>Delivery guide</h3><p>The timetable, room plan, participant rotations, team responsibilities and preparation checklist.</p></article>
<article class="item"><div class="sheet"><span class="stamp">Sample</span><div class="sh-t">One-Page Profile</div><div class="sh-s">Sample Participant · Customer Advisor</div><div class="sh-box"><strong>Recommendation:</strong> proceed, with a focused first 90 days.</div><div class="sh-l">Evidence</div><table class="st"><tr><td>Group case</td><td class="dots">●●●○</td></tr><tr><td>Role play</td><td class="dots">●●●●</td></tr><tr><td>Interview notes</td><td class="dots">●●●○</td></tr></table><div class="sh-l">Gap to explore</div><p style="font-size:11px;color:inherit">Linking product features to value.</p></div><h3>One-page profile</h3><p>A report template showing the recommendation, evidence, gaps and onboarding priorities.</p></article>
</div>
<div class="work"><svg class="scene" viewBox="0 0 240 150" role="img" aria-label="A facilitator explaining a chart"><g stroke="#2c2a26" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" fill="none"><rect x="14" y="14" width="124" height="82" rx="3" fill="#fff"/><circle cx="60" cy="48" r="20" fill="#f8dc8c"/><circle cx="88" cy="48" r="20" fill="#f3dfb0" fill-opacity=".8"/><circle cx="74" cy="66" r="20" fill="#cfe0c9" fill-opacity=".8"/><path d="M76 96v40M50 136l26-18 26 18"/><circle cx="182" cy="43.9" r="9.9" fill="#fff"/><path d="M164.4 84.6v-8.8a17.6 17.6 0 0 1 35.2 0v8.8z" fill="#f8dc8c"/><path d="M164 72l-22-14"/><path d="M10 138h220"/></g></svg><div><h3>Assessor workshop</h3><p>A one-day workshop that trains your assessors in what to look for, how to record evidence, how to score and how to reach a fair shared judgement.</p></div></div>
<p class="note">Blank samples of the scoring sheet and summary are available on request. Full scripts are shared after appointment.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="section evi"><div class="wrap"><svg class="sec-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-panel"/></svg><div class="eyebrow">From evidence to decision</div><h2>A clear path to a confident decision.</h2>
<ol class="flow">
<li><svg class="f-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-speech"/></svg><span class="mini">Before the day</span><h3>Interview</h3><p>Your team covers motivation, experience and essentials, then shares its notes.</p></li>
<li><svg class="f-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-podium"/></svg><span class="mini">The day</span><h3>Exercises</h3><p>The group case and role play add evidence of how each person works.</p></li>
<li><svg class="f-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-panel"/></svg><span class="mini">Same day</span><h3>Calibration</h3><p>The panel rates each source first, then agrees one view against the role.</p></li>
<li><svg class="f-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-profile"/></svg><span class="mini">Afterwards</span><h3>Profile</h3><p>A one-page summary of the recommendation, evidence and priorities.</p></li>
<li><svg class="f-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-flag"/></svg><span class="mini">Your decision</span><h3>Next step</h3><p>Your hiring manager reviews the evidence and makes the final decision.</p></li>
</ol><p class="line-note">A follow-up conversation is only needed where a specific evidence gap remains.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap"><svg class="sec-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-puzzle"/></svg><div class="eyebrow">Ways to work together</div><h2>Keep the capability in your organisation.</h2><p class="intro">Choose how much you want POV to do. The goal is a centre that fits your organisation and that your team can trust and use.</p>
<div class="opts">
<article class="opt"><h3>Design &amp; Equip</h3><p>We design the materials, review the case with your team and train your assessors to run the centre.</p></article>
<article class="opt"><h3>Design &amp; Deliver</h3><p>We design the centre and deliver it with you, including facilitation, assessment, calibration and summaries.</p></article>
<article class="opt"><h3>Review &amp; Refine</h3><p>We observe a centre you already run, share feedback and strengthen it.</p></article>
</div><p class="line-note">A fast-track plan can reach the assessor workshop in about nine working days, depending on your inputs and availability.</p></div></section>
